WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.270
To understand experimental results,
it's essential to get a feel for some

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.920
common graphs and what they mean. We
will look at line graphs, histograms,

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.890
and dot plots. Let's take an
experimental example from ecology. How

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:19.750
does the number of rabbits change with
time? With unlimited food, the number

5
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.190
of rabbits increases exponentially with
time. The amount of rabbits simply

6
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:29.370
depends on how long they have been
reproducing. But if there is a limited

7
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.950
rate of food production, grass growth,
the number of rabbits will increase to

8
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:39.220
a maximum population size, where they
begin to starve. What if we plot the

9
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.860
maximum number of rabbits as a function
of the rate of grass growth? Now we get

10
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:49.830
a straight line. Now we are curious
about how rabbit body mass varies with

11
00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.140
limited food. For this, we can use a
histogram.

12
00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:00.220
The Y axis of a histogram is frequency
and, here, the X axis is the body mass

13
00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:04.860
of rabbits. Histograms can have a
normal distribution, a skewed

14
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.490
distribution, or a bimodal distribution.
If we look at rabbit body mass, we see

15
00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:12.530
that this distribution is bimodal.

16
00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:19.450
There are fat rabbits and thin rabbits
but not much in between. So why are

17
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.840
some rabbits fat and others thin?

18
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.620
Let's use a dot plot to investigate.
Here we will examine how age on the Y

19
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:35.070
axis relates to body mass on the X axis.
Now we find that fat rabbits are

20
00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:39.840
usually middle aged, but there are two
types of skinny bunnies: young fast

21
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.680
ones and old sickly ones. Perhaps young
bunnies hop a lot, burn calories and

22
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.050
stay thin. Old bunnies could be too
slow to get new grass so they starve.

23
00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.250
Further observations will be needed to
test these hypotheses.

